 This file is a working draft of QueryGate's intended Business Source License
 1.1 terms. It has NOT been reviewed or settled by a lawyer, the Licensor
 legal entity named below does not exist yet, and the Change Date has not been
 stamped. Nothing in this file is legal advice, and no one should rely on it
 as QueryGate's licence until this banner is removed.

 WHAT GOVERNS IN THE MEANTIME: this draft grants nothing. Until the banner is
 removed, QueryGate remains proprietary and all rights are reserved — the terms
 previously carried by this file, and the EULA in docs/legal/EULA.en.md /
 docs/legal/EULA.he.md, continue to govern. The repository is private; no
 public licence is granted by the presence of this draft.

 Four values are unknown and are left as literal placeholders below. The
 Licensor placeholder appears twice (the parameter and the copyright line) and
 both must be filled together; the alternative-licensing line needs a real
 channel, not a company name, so it is its own placeholder:
   * <LICENSOR — legal entity, to be supplied>          (x2)
   * <LICENSING_CONTACT — email address or URL>
   * <VERSION — stamped per release>
   * <CHANGE_DATE — stamped per release>
 Change Date stamping is a separate, later work package; see docs/RELEASING.md.

 Drafting notes for counsel: docs/LICENSE_NOTES.md
 Plain-language explanation for users: docs/LICENSING_FAQ.md

 On this banner itself: the "Covenants of Licensor" below (covenant 4) require
 the Licensor not to modify the License text in any other way. This banner sits
 outside the License text and modifies none of it, but it must be deleted
 before the licence goes into force regardless — see docs/LICENSE_NOTES.md.
